<document xmlns="http://cnx.rice.edu/cnxml" xmlns:m="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML">
  <title>6.2.3: Multiplying a Polynomial by a Polynomial</title>
  <metadata xmlns:md="http://cnx.rice.edu/mdml">
    <md:content-id>m01595</md:content-id>
    <md:title>6.2.3: Multiplying a Polynomial by a Polynomial</md:title>
    <md:uuid>d67cb33b-8c5c-4fd9-860d-47ad3a331d81</md:uuid>
  </metadata>
  <content>
  <section><para>For questions 1 - 5, match each polynomial expression to its simplified solution. Be prepared to explain or show your work.</para>
<!-- BEGIN ACTIVITY DROP DOWN 1 TRY -->
<section class="check-understanding"><title>Activity</title><exercise data-content-id="99fecd6c-c3ad-440d-b80f-2c9a69d3347f"><problem><para>
      <para>\((c+1)(c^2+3c+6)\) </para>
      </para></problem><solution><para>𝑐³+4𝑐²+9𝑐+6</para><para>
      <para>Nice try! The correct answer is \(c^3+4c^2+9c+6\).</para>
    </para></solution></exercise></section><!--END ACTIVITY DROP DOWN 1 TRY -->

<!-- BEGIN CLICK TO REVEAL NO TEXTBOX -->

<!--Q#6-->
<example><exercise>
  <problem>
    
    <para>Now, fill in the missing blanks to complete the polynomial multiplication.
        \(\begin{array}{rcl}\left(2x-4\right)\left(x^2+\square x-5\right)&amp;=&amp;2x\left(x^2+6x-5\right)-4\left(x^2+6x-\square\right)\\&amp;=&amp;2x^3+\square x^2-10x-4x^2-24x+\square\\&amp;=&amp;\square x^3+8x^2-\square x+20\end{array}\)
      </para>
    <para>Write down your answer, then select the <emphasis>solution</emphasis> button to compare your work.</para>
  </problem><solution>
  <para>Compare your answer:</para>
  <para>\(\begin{array}{rcl}\left(2x-4\right)\left(x^2+6x-5\right)&amp;=&amp;2x\left(x^2+6x-5\right)-4\left(x^2+6x-5\right)\\&amp;=&amp;2x^3+12x^2-10x-4x^2-24x+20\\&amp;=&amp;2x^3+8x^2-34x+20\end{array}\)</para>
</solution></exercise>
</example><!--Interaction End -->

<!-- END CLICK TO REVEAL NO TEXTBOX -->
